Z||000041||Black88GT||08-31-2000||10:29 PM||||5 amps in the trunk? Yeah right.  As almost everyone knows, it gets VERY hot in the trunk.  EVEN IF you could cram in 5 amps, they would have no air, and they would overheat and fry themselves.  I had ONE amp in my trunk and it was a pain to run the wires of the amp and keeping it cool was a pain.  I would have to see pics to believe that one.  If you are pushing 2 twelves, 1 eight, one ten, and 6x9s, you would need some reasonably powered amps.  Most amps with more then 200 total watts take up about 12 inches x 13 inches, if not more. Like I said, I need pics to believe that one.  How did you run the wires?  With 5 amps you surely have a crossover, where did you put that when you already have 5 amps in the trunk, 1 ten in the front compartment, and 2 twelves behind the seats (that too is VERY hard to custom build)<P><BR>sorry to be a doubting Thomas but...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||4
