Z||000049||Pontiaddict||09-01-2000||04:05 PM||||You'll post pics of the speakers in the Lexus, but not the turbos in the Fiero.<P>A 12 speaker stereo is easy, 2 in the dash, 2 in each headrest with the early seats, 1 per sail panel, put 2 in the vent grilles for the computer, factory sub, and a real speaker anywhere else. <P>The bottom of my trunk gets wet because the weatherstrip is bad, not a good place to put amps.<P>If the turbos are sitting in your trunk, why can't you use them on the Northstar? (I know why, but answer anyway.)||||reg||1
Z||000050||Pontiaddict||09-01-2000||04:11 PM||||You'll post pics of the speakers in the Lexus, but not the turbos in the Fiero.<P>A 12 speaker stereo is easy, 2 in the dash, 2 in each headrest with the early seats, 1 per sail panel, put 2 in the vent grilles for the computer, factory sub, and a real speaker anywhere else. <P>The bottom of my trunk gets wet because the weatherstrip is bad, not a good place to put amps.<P>If the turbos are sitting in your trunk, why can't you use them on the Northstar? (I know why, but answer anyway.)||||reg||1
Z||000051||Seanh||09-01-2000||05:40 PM||||Like iv said before, I install these stero systems everyday. You may be able to slaughter me on the enigine and stuff like that. But hey, Ill tell you everything about this system. Someone asked how I fit an 8" in the 5.25 in hole? Do you really think I used the factory sealed box? I purchased the boxes behind the seats and the one upfront and the 8" REPLACMENT to the factory box, and also the Midranges compartments from <A HREF="http://www.subbox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.subbox.com</A>  they sell boxes for Fieros. All the system amps and Premier PRS-Silver Series. 2 PRS-X720's, 2 PRS-X320, one GM-X644. check the sizes for them at <A HREF="http://www.pioneerelectronics.com" TARGET=_blank>www.pioneerelectronics.com</A>  and go to Premier Car Audio page. They fit end to end with those specs on there so they mounted in the trunk with no space problems. I did figure out that the North* would change the trunk, but I could always mount them somewhere else if I go that option. Heat is not a problem because there are 2 fans on the top of the amp compartment in the trunk, blowing in opposite directions. The bottem of the trunk is vented to the outside and the trunk is lined with 2 layers of Theroinsulation. If you would like to see that information go to <A HREF="http://www.phoenixgold.com." TARGET=_blank>www.phoenixgold.com.</A>  <BR>The Lexus is an ES250. Sorry about that<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Currently upgrading to a NorthStar.||||reg||1
