Z||000055||EdsB52||09-02-2000||02:40 AM||||I think I'll jump into the "pack of dog" mentality here, sounds like fun! ........ES, GT, whatever, they're all the same. I own four pieces crap for vehicles and I know all the designations for them. I know all the displacements, etc. I find it ironic that Shaun can whip off stereo part numbers, but doesn't know the designation of his alleged used $20,000 car. I've built 2 computers with the help of a friend. I'm no where near a pro, but I understand the names of the various components, what they do, and in general what is compatible with each other. Even my jap-car driving girlfriend knows she drives a 200sx, not a 200 sx ser. She also knows it is basically a Sentra with fancy wheels. She knows it has a 1.6L, not the 2.0L. What I'm getting at is that people tend have a grasp of what they have and Shaun is blowing smoke. But to be objective, fifty some posts busting his nuts is exactly what he wants. Compulsive liars desire this attention, so, as the rest of you, I've fallen victim to this sicko. Let's just not take him seriously or reply to his rhetoric.<P>Another point. I love cranking Metalica Black album until my ears bleed, at least as much as anyone in this forum. But why would anyone need 12 speaks in approx 20 sq feet (guess) of space? I don't doubt that it could be done, but WTF?||||reg||1
