Z||000061||Seanh||09-02-2000||10:16 PM||||A little more about that subbox. It is 1.1 ft sealed enclosure. You have to cut the bottem of the spare tire pod out because the box sits in there. A 23" to 27" long port tube(depending on how high you want to place it in the floor) goes in the pass. side floor boards. It is 4" in dia. The box holds a 10" sub in a bandpass type enclosure. I put a Polk Audio Momo series sub in there, and Amped it at 400 RMS, and 800 max. It sounds very good with all types of music also. It sounds more like I have an 18 up there. website is <A HREF="http://www.subbox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.subbox.com</A>  there a little pricy, but I now see that there well worth it. They have some pics of the box and tubes.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Currently upgrading to a NorthStar.||||reg||1
Z||000062||baldlobo||09-03-2000||12:52 AM||||So what I'm jumping on the band wagon here so here's my rant. I think our friend here with the supposed vehicles is pulling our collective chains because all I found that could posibly match his supposed Lexus is ES250 and it was built in 1991-1992 so unless our little friend here can give us a vin we can check, I wouldn't believe a word he said.<P>||||reg||5
Z||000063||stimpy||09-03-2000||09:00 AM||||Why would a custom stereo shop that does competition insalls on a daily basis need to order an enclosure from subbox.com? And while perusing the subbox website, why do I not see<BR>the bhind the seat enclosures for the alleged 12"s? Why am I still asking rhetorical questions? Why are we still reading this bullshit? <P>Cliff, please put a lock on this cesspool of BS, before I loose my cool and say something mean to this punk and get everyone mad at me! <P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000064||Seanh||09-03-2000||09:19 AM||||The design for that sealed box is extremly difficult and since I only work on the Fiero After shop hours, I decided that it would be easier to buy it. Sure, Ill get ya that VIN number today. Its at the shop, but if it will make you happy Ill go get it. And the boxes that hold the subs behind the seats were ones I asked him to custom build. Go ahead and email him to ask if he has done it. <P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Currently upgrading to a NorthStar.||||reg||1
