Z||000099||Black88GT||09-04-2000||01:35 PM||||I still want to see pics of these 5 amps in the trunk.  And that was a good point whoever brought up that thing about if this guy works at a stereo shop why doesn't he build it himself?  That B.S. excuse of "I don't have time" just ain't cuttin it.  That enclosure sold at subbox.com would be easy to custom build for someone who supposedly has experience in the department.  Just doesn't sound right to me.  Unless you went through all the work that fierosound (i think it was him) did with the 12" behind the seats, you would have to have the seats all the way up.  I guess that would work if your 4 feet tall.  PLUS there is still the wire issue.  I don't see how you could run those wires without them melting.  Finally, the heat issue.  You said you cut a hole and used a metal port for the amp wires to run through, well that would let even more heat into the trunk.  With 5 amps in an enclosed trunk with the heat of an engine coming in, your amps would be F-R-I-E-D.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||13
